# The data of a launch may be an anonymous Structure written in parentheses (R21, item 4; plan M11 5b): it is that
# Structure as written, given by name to the record of a launch by name and as an operand of the receiver call -- in a
# callable's code and at the root. As the only positional argument of a record it is read by P0 as the record's tail
# (`Add((int: v 7))` is `Add: int: v 7`), whose one field is a place.
Total:
    int: sum 0
end: Total
Add:
    Total\sum := Total\sum + v
end: Add
fn: f () int
    Add(data := (int: v 5))
    call((int: v 3); Add)
    return: Total\sum
end: f
int: seen f()
call((int: v 4); Add)
int: after Total\sum
